Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:47:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(session): isolate non-JSON projection units instead of
 failing the record
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A single unit whose state violates the plain-JSON contract (e.g. a
third-party plugin's contextTimeline initial state with undefined fields)
previously failed the whole checkpoint serialization. The write path is
fail-soft, so the failure was silent: every session's cache row stopped
updating, and after an environment restart the sidebar history showed each
session's workspace title instead of its task title until the session was
clicked.

put() now snapshots per unit: a violating row is dropped with a warning and
the surviving rows still land; when nothing survives the pass, the previous
record is kept rather than replaced with an empty one. A dropped key reads
as not-yet-available and refolds from the log on the next fuller read —
the same degradation a lost write already costs, now bounded to the broken
unit instead of evicting the whole session's cache (titles etc. persist).

The cache suite gains two cases (a bad unit's row is dropped while a good
unit's value still lands and is served by cachedSnapshot; an all-bad
checkpoint keeps the previous record). End-to-end probes reproduce the
original failure (dsh-context mounted: put threw, cold cachedSnapshot
empty) and confirm the fix (write succeeds, title survives the cold
snapshot, the full host session.list cold path serves the title).
